(1978403, 271660, 18349, '<td valign="top">This is breathtaking.  If I had any suggestions for improvement, it might be to crop about 3/4" or so off the top so it''s not so "heavy" up there, but other than that, it''s gorgeous.  :)</td>', 'This is breathtaking.  If I had any suggestions for improvement, it might be to crop about 3/4" or so off the top so it''s not so "heavy" up there, but other than that, it''s gorgeous.  :)', '2005-12-26 07:53:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(1978408, 272005, 18349, '<td valign="top">I''m not sure I understand the message presented.  The photo itself, IMHO, is cluttered with a lot of info that is either extraneous or confusing.  The red out-of-focus element in the foreground is more of a distraction than anything (is it a shoe?) and the hot spots on that same element really pull the eye away from the figure, which is what I assume is the main subject.  The image is not evenly-lit, which is a bit distracting as well, especially in the background.   The blown-out area on the left contrasts a bit too heavily with the darker area on the right.  The texture on the wall is a bit of a distracting element as well.  If you could seperate the subject from the background more, it would be smoother and more pleasing to the eye.   Please take my critique with a grain of salt, because I am no pro.  I just wanted to offer my immediate thoughts.</td>', 'I''m not sure I understand the message presented.  The photo itself, IMHO, is cluttered with a lot of info that is either extraneous or confusing.  The red out-of-focus element in the foreground is more of a distraction than anything (is it a shoe?) and the hot spots on that same element really pull the eye away from the figure, which is what I assume is the main subject.  The image is not evenly-lit, which is a bit distracting as well, especially in the background.   The blown-out area on the left contrasts a bit too heavily with the darker area on the right.  The texture on the wall is a bit of a distracting element as well.  If you could seperate the subject from the background more, it would be smoother and more pleasing to the eye.   Please take my critique with a grain of salt, because I am no pro.  I just wanted to offer my immediate thoughts.', '2005-12-26 07:59:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(1978412, 271922, 18349, '<td valign="top">This is very nice, with a good tonal range and clarity.  I''d suggest putting the feather more on the diagonal in the frame, to lead the viewer''s eye from one corner to the other, through the entire width of the image...as it is, the eye just moves up and stops abruptly, leaving the viewer wanting to see more that isn''t there.  Like I said, though, it''s very nice all the same.  :)</td>', 'This is very nice, with a good tonal range and clarity.  I''d suggest putting the feather more on the diagonal in the frame, to lead the viewer''s eye from one corner to the other, through the entire width of the image...as it is, the eye just moves up and stops abruptly, leaving the viewer wanting to see more that isn''t there.  Like I said, though, it''s very nice all the same.  :)', '2005-12-26 08:06:45.000000', NULL, 1),
