(1999906, 271660, 27735, '<td valign="top">Although I don''t care whether or not this shot is original, I agree that the technical quality isn''t that great. For me, the photo doesn''t look sharp and there are too many artifacts. It is a great composition and exposure, though, and the majority of voters thought it was the best of the challenge. You should be thrilled with that. Just my 2 cents...<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by anusaha:</b></div><hr/><i> This is <i>not original at all</i>. I thought the image looked familiar...I used to have this as a background back in high school. A quick image search confirmed this is an over-photographed site. Originality aside, I can''t say I''m impressed by the technical quality either.<br/><a href="//images.google.com/images?q=%22Mesa+Arch%22&amp;hl=en" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//images.google.com/images?q=%22Mesa+Arch%22&amp;hl=en</a> </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'Although I don''t care whether or not this shot is original, I agree that the technical quality isn''t that great. For me, the photo doesn''t look sharp and there are too many artifacts. It is a great composition and exposure, though, and the majority of voters thought it was the best of the challenge. You should be thrilled with that. Just my 2 cents... Originally posted by anusaha: This is not original at all. I thought the image looked familiar...I used to have this as a background back in high school. A quick image search confirmed this is an over-photographed site. Originality aside, I can''t say I''m impressed by the technical quality either.//images.google.com/images?q=%22Mesa+Arch%22&hl=en ', '2006-01-03 21:26:03.000000', NULL, 0),
