(2002872, 271488, 39664, '<td valign="top">You are one of the most amazing photographers on this site!  I would have thought this was deserving of the blue also.  Maybe people are getting too familiar with your work and not being as generous with their scores because you are so damn good!  I''d give it a 10+ everytime!</td>', 'You are one of the most amazing photographers on this site!  I would have thought this was deserving of the blue also.  Maybe people are getting too familiar with your work and not being as generous with their scores because you are so damn good!  I''d give it a 10+ everytime!', '2006-01-04 12:38:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(2002983, 271488, 37053, '<td valign="top">Wonderful picture, you continue to be one of my favorite photographers.  You work is truely great.<br/> <br/>The only thing I wan''t so keen on in this picture was the black background.  It seemed to blend a bit too much with her outfit and made it feel a bit more like a stage shot.<br/> <br/>I didn''t get a chance to vote on this challenge but I would have voted this one highest.  Congrats on another ribbon!</td>', 'Wonderful picture, you continue to be one of my favorite photographers.  You work is truely great. The only thing I wan''t so keen on in this picture was the black background.  It seemed to blend a bit too much with her outfit and made it feel a bit more like a stage shot. I didn''t get a chance to vote on this challenge but I would have voted this one highest.  Congrats on another ribbon!', '2006-01-04 13:04:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(2003044, 272463, 45524, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique club. First off let me congratulate you on an amazing shot. I really like this. Although I didnt vote this challenge, I would have scored it an 8 or 9. As far as why it didnt score very well, alot of voters may not know that the sibject is named weaver, BTW I beleive that is a Southern Masked weaver, but thats not your fault. Now on to the critique.<br/> <br/>Great compostion, very good focus, and I love the colors. SHallow DOF works very well here. The only thing I might have sugested was bumping the color up a bit. I think the voters really like colors that flash and jump out to them, maybe play with the hue or saturation on the yellow and make the bird jump out a bit. Overall a great job, and I am kind of surprised it didnt score above 6. Good luck on future challenges.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique club. First off let me congratulate you on an amazing shot. I really like this. Although I didnt vote this challenge, I would have scored it an 8 or 9. As far as why it didnt score very well, alot of voters may not know that the sibject is named weaver, BTW I beleive that is a Southern Masked weaver, but thats not your fault. Now on to the critique. Great compostion, very good focus, and I love the colors. SHallow DOF works very well here. The only thing I might have sugested was bumping the color up a bit. I think the voters really like colors that flash and jump out to them, maybe play with the hue or saturation on the yellow and make the bird jump out a bit. Overall a great job, and I am kind of surprised it didnt score above 6. Good luck on future challenges.', '2006-01-04 13:19:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(2003199, 272613, 47117, '<td valign="top">Angela, LOL....I''m sorry for the low votes and the comments you seemed to dislike from me on them in the past - hence this image I imagine. But your lack of close attention to detail again shows in the transposing of the numbers. Therefore, my comments remain unaltered.  I am glad you got a chance to vent though! LMAO....</td>', 'Angela, LOL....I''m sorry for the low votes and the comments you seemed to dislike from me on them in the past - hence this image I imagine. But your lack of close attention to detail again shows in the transposing of the numbers. Therefore, my comments remain unaltered.  I am glad you got a chance to vent though! LMAO....', '2006-01-04 13:50:33.000000', NULL, 0),
