(2013372, 271660, 18367, '<td valign="top">This is an absolutely breathtaking image.  I gave it a well deserved 10 and in all likelyhood would have voted it even higher had I been given an opportunity to do so.  I shall assume  by the lighting that you took this image in the latter part of the day.  <br/> <br/>Stunning capture that makes me want to pay a visit to your part of the world.  I remain confident that an image of this  quality posted of a travel brochure would entice people to visit the Canyonlands National Park... I know it does for me, and I will.<br/> <br/>Ray<br/> <br/></td>', 'This is an absolutely breathtaking image.  I gave it a well deserved 10 and in all likelyhood would have voted it even higher had I been given an opportunity to do so.  I shall assume  by the lighting that you took this image in the latter part of the day.   Stunning capture that makes me want to pay a visit to your part of the world.  I remain confident that an image of this  quality posted of a travel brochure would entice people to visit the Canyonlands National Park... I know it does for me, and I will. Ray ', '2006-01-07 18:27:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(2013498, 271660, 10397, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by RayEthier:</b></div><hr/><i> This is an absolutely breathtaking image.  I gave it a well deserved 10 and in all likelyhood would have voted it even higher had I been given an opportunity to do so.  I shall assume  by the lighting that you took this image in the latter part of the day.  <br/> <br/>Stunning capture that makes me want to pay a visit to your part of the world.  I remain confident that an image of this  quality posted of a travel brochure would entice people to visit the Canyonlands National Park... I know it does for me, and I will.<br/> <br/>Ray </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Ray,<br/> <br/>Thanks for the compliment!! If you go to Canyonlands to shoot Mesa Arch, get there very early in the morning. When it''s still dark (5am), and stay until at least 10am. Sunrise is the only time of day to shoot this arch.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-01-07 20:26:02.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by RayEthier: This is an absolutely breathtaking image.  I gave it a well deserved 10 and in all likelyhood would have voted it even higher had I been given an opportunity to do so.  I shall assume  by the lighting that you took this image in the latter part of the day.   Stunning capture that makes me want to pay a visit to your part of the world.  I remain confident that an image of this  quality posted of a travel brochure would entice people to visit the Canyonlands National Park... I know it does for me, and I will. Ray   Ray, Thanks for the compliment!! If you go to Canyonlands to shoot Mesa Arch, get there very early in the morning. When it''s still dark (5am), and stay until at least 10am. Sunrise is the only time of day to shoot this arch.', '2006-01-07 20:24:42.000000', '2006-01-07 20:26:02.000000', 0),
