(2160465, 272556, 37893, '<td valign="top">I like the starkness of this image. there is enough detail in the branches to make out what is happening yet there is also a sense of depth by the shadows and tonalities overall. I agree with teh left side being ta tad too dark though. This is a nice image that I''m sure you''re proud of capturing ;)</td>', 'I like the starkness of this image. there is enough detail in the branches to make out what is happening yet there is also a sense of depth by the shadows and tonalities overall. I agree with teh left side being ta tad too dark though. This is a nice image that I''m sure you''re proud of capturing ;)', '2006-02-18 01:52:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(2186164, 271660, 53964, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by anusaha:</b></div><hr/><i> This is <i>not original at all</i>. I thought the image looked familiar...I used to have this as a background back in high school. A quick image search confirmed this is an over-photographed site. Originality aside, I can''t say I''m impressed by the technical quality either.<br/><a href="//images.google.com/images?q=%22Mesa+Arch%22&amp;hl=en" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//images.google.com/images?q=%22Mesa+Arch%22&amp;hl=en</a> </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>So, does that mean landmark pics, no matter how spectacular, are taboo just because someone, somewhere, has at some time taken a picture of/from the same thing? I''ve seen shots of this before too, but I LOVE this one.  No two photos are ever alike.....<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by anusaha: This is not original at all. I thought the image looked familiar...I used to have this as a background back in high school. A quick image search confirmed this is an over-photographed site. Originality aside, I can''t say I''m impressed by the technical quality either.//images.google.com/images?q=%22Mesa+Arch%22&hl=en   So, does that mean landmark pics, no matter how spectacular, are taboo just because someone, somewhere, has at some time taken a picture of/from the same thing? I''ve seen shots of this before too, but I LOVE this one.  No two photos are ever alike.....', '2006-02-27 04:18:43.000000', NULL, 0),
