(2673922, 272622, 62755, '<td valign="top">I like the shot quite a bit... but would have used a second curtain sync with the flash - cause now it looks like he is going backwards. Otherwise a great shot.</td>', 'I like the shot quite a bit... but would have used a second curtain sync with the flash - cause now it looks like he is going backwards. Otherwise a great shot.', '2006-07-29 13:28:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(2676264, 271660, 35970, '<td valign="top">This is an excellent interpretation of Mesa Arch, Canyonlands National Park &amp; the La Sal mountains. Looking at the big collection of photos taken of this site "Mesa Arch", it appears that each photographer sees it differently. It almost makes me want to run out there myself and take a look. How can one spot get so many different interpretations? It is facinating. What I like about this photograph is that there seems to be a balance of form and size that is artistically finished. And more importantly, it creates a feeling a "being there and looking out" as opposed to just a photo of a heavy arched rock. The heaviness is gone and the landscape intrigues the eye.</td>', 'This is an excellent interpretation of Mesa Arch, Canyonlands National Park & the La Sal mountains. Looking at the big collection of photos taken of this site "Mesa Arch", it appears that each photographer sees it differently. It almost makes me want to run out there myself and take a look. How can one spot get so many different interpretations? It is facinating. What I like about this photograph is that there seems to be a balance of form and size that is artistically finished. And more importantly, it creates a feeling a "being there and looking out" as opposed to just a photo of a heavy arched rock. The heaviness is gone and the landscape intrigues the eye.', '2006-07-30 15:33:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(2695463, 272448, 60862, '<td valign="top">Thanks for showing how to take everday items and make an eye-grabbing picture.<br/> <br/>In particular, the off-center shot.  Many people here score in the low 5s and upper 4s partly because they put together something with potential and then shoot it straight on.<br/> <br/>The angle here not only makes it more visually interesting, but it gives the illusion of being a 3-D amusement park ride. :)</td>', 'Thanks for showing how to take everday items and make an eye-grabbing picture. In particular, the off-center shot.  Many people here score in the low 5s and upper 4s partly because they put together something with potential and then shoot it straight on. The angle here not only makes it more visually interesting, but it gives the illusion of being a 3-D amusement park ride. :)', '2006-08-04 14:52:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(2733691, 272253, 34659, '<td valign="top">This is soooo good!  The focus, color, and lighting control is just perfect.  Such a playful pose too.  You really captured her well!</td>', 'This is soooo good!  The focus, color, and lighting control is just perfect.  Such a playful pose too.  You really captured her well!', '2006-08-16 12:38:34.000000', NULL, 0),
